# Fuel.me Interview Project - AI Assistant Context

## Project Overview

This is a monorepo for a technical interview with Fuel.me. Built for speed and type safety.

**Time constraint: 60 minutes for feature implementation**

## Architecture

### Monorepo Structure

```
fuel-me-interview-prep/
├── apps/
│   ├── backend/          # NestJS API (Port 4000)
│   ├── site-manager/     # Public React app (Port 3000)
│   └── dispatcher/       # Admin React app (Port 3001)
└── packages/
    └── shared/           # Shared TypeScript types
```

### Tech Stack

- **Frontend**: React 18 + Vite + TypeScript (strict) + TailwindCSS
- **Backend**: NestJS + TypeScript (strict) + Prisma ORM
- **Database**: PostgreSQL 16 (Docker)
- **Package Manager**: pnpm workspaces
- **Validation**: class-validator, class-transformer
- **Linting**: ESLint (strict, zero errors)

## Critical Patterns

### 1. Type-First Development

**ALWAYS start with types in the shared package**

```typescript
// packages/shared/src/index.ts
export interface MyEntity {
  id: string;
  name: string;
  status: "active" | "inactive";
  createdAt: string;
}

export interface CreateMyEntityDto {
  name: string;
  status?: "active" | "inactive";
}
```

After adding types:

```bash
pnpm --filter shared build
```

### 2. Database Schema (Prisma)

Add to `apps/backend/prisma/schema.prisma`:

```prisma
model MyEntity {
  id        String   @id @default(uuid())
  name      String
  status    String   @default("active")
  createdAt DateTime @default(now())
  updatedAt DateTime @updatedAt

  @@map("my_entities")
}
```

Create table manually (due to Prisma permissions issue):

```bash
docker exec fuel-me-postgres psql -U postgres -d fuel_me_dev -c "
CREATE TABLE my_entities (
  id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,
  name TEXT NOT NULL,
  status TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'active',
  \"createdAt\" TIMESTAMP NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,
  \"updatedAt\" TIMESTAMP NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
);"
```

### 3. Backend Implementation (NestJS)

**Module** (`apps/backend/src/my-entity/my-entity.module.ts`):

```typescript
import { Module } from "@nestjs/common";
import { MyEntityController } from "./my-entity.controller";
import { MyEntityService } from "./my-entity.service";
import { PrismaService } from "../prisma.service";

@Module({
  controllers: [MyEntityController],
  providers: [MyEntityService, PrismaService],
})
export class MyEntityModule {}
```

**Controller** (`apps/backend/src/my-entity/my-entity.controller.ts`):

```typescript
import { Controller, Get, Post, Body, Param } from "@nestjs/common";
import { MyEntityService } from "./my-entity.service";
import type { MyEntity, CreateMyEntityDto } from "shared";

@Controller("my-entities")
export class MyEntityController {
  constructor(private readonly service: MyEntityService) {}

  @Get()
  findAll(): Promise<MyEntity[]> {
    return this.service.findAll();
  }

  @Get(":id")
  findOne(@Param("id") id: string): Promise<MyEntity | null> {
    return this.service.findOne(id);
  }

  @Post()
  create(@Body() dto: CreateMyEntityDto): Promise<MyEntity> {
    return this.service.create(dto);
  }
}
```

**Service** (`apps/backend/src/my-entity/my-entity.service.ts`):

```typescript
import { Injectable } from "@nestjs/common";
import { PrismaService } from "../prisma.service";
import type { MyEntity, CreateMyEntityDto } from "shared";

@Injectable()
export class MyEntityService {
  constructor(private prisma: PrismaService) {}

  async findAll(): Promise<MyEntity[]> {
    const entities = await this.prisma.myEntity.findMany({
      orderBy: { createdAt: "desc" },
    });
    return entities.map(this.toDto);
  }

  async findOne(id: string): Promise<MyEntity | null> {
    const entity = await this.prisma.myEntity.findUnique({ where: { id } });
    return entity ? this.toDto(entity) : null;
  }

  async create(dto: CreateMyEntityDto): Promise<MyEntity> {
    const entity = await this.prisma.myEntity.create({
      data: {
        id: crypto.randomUUID(),
        ...dto,
      },
    });
    return this.toDto(entity);
  }

  private toDto(entity: any): MyEntity {
    return {
      ...entity,
      createdAt: entity.createdAt.toISOString(),
      updatedAt: entity.updatedAt.toISOString(),
    };
  }
}
```

**Register in AppModule** (`apps/backend/src/app.module.ts`):

```typescript
import { MyEntityModule } from './my-entity/my-entity.module';

@Module({
  imports: [MyEntityModule],
  // ...
})
```

### 4. Frontend Implementation

**Site Manager** (`apps/site-manager/src/components/MyEntityList.tsx`):

```typescript
import { useState, useEffect } from 'react';
import type { MyEntity } from 'shared';

const API_URL = 'http://localhost:4000';

export function MyEntityList() {
  const [entities, setEntities] = useState<MyEntity[]>([]);
  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(true);
  const [error, setError] = useState<string | null>(null);

  useEffect(() => {
    fetch(`${API_URL}/my-entities`)
      .then(res => res.json())
      .then(data => {
        setEntities(data);
        setLoading(false);
      })
      .catch(err => {
        setError(err.message);
        setLoading(false);
      });
  }, []);

  if (loading) return <div className="text-center py-4">Loading...</div>;
  if (error) return <div className="text-red-500 py-4">Error: {error}</div>;

  return (
    <div className="space-y-4">
      <h2 className="text-2xl font-bold">My Entities</h2>
      <div className="grid gap-4">
        {entities.map(entity => (
          <div key={entity.id} className="border rounded-lg p-4">
            <h3 className="font-semibold">{entity.name}</h3>
            <p className="text-sm text-gray-500">{entity.status}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  );
}
```

**Dispatcher** (similar but with admin-focused UI):

```typescript
// apps/dispatcher/src/components/MyEntityAdmin.tsx
// Add create/edit forms, bulk actions, etc.
```

## Speed Optimization Tips

### Creating a Complete Feature (5-minute workflow)

1. **Types First** (1 min):

   ```bash
   # Edit packages/shared/src/index.ts
   pnpm --filter shared build
   ```

2. **Database** (1 min):

   ```bash
   # Add to apps/backend/prisma/schema.prisma
   # Create table via docker exec (see pattern above)
   ```

3. **Backend** (2 min):

   ```bash
   # Create module, controller, service
   # Register in AppModule
   ```

4. **Frontend** (1 min):
   ```bash
   # Create component in both apps
   # Import and use
   ```

### Useful Commands

```bash
# Start everything
pnpm dev

# Lint (must pass)
pnpm lint

# Build shared types
pnpm --filter shared build

# Generate Prisma client
pnpm --filter backend db:generate

# Create table manually
docker exec fuel-me-postgres psql -U postgres -d fuel_me_dev -c "SQL_HERE"

# Kill ports if needed
lsof -ti:4000 | xargs kill -9
lsof -ti:3000 | xargs kill -9
lsof -ti:3001 | xargs kill -9
```

## Database Setup

**Connection Details:**

- Host: localhost
- Port: 5432
- Database: fuel_me_dev
- User: postgres
- Password: postgres

**Important Note:**
Due to a Prisma permissions issue, create tables manually using `docker exec`. The pattern is:

- Define model in Prisma schema
- Create table via psql command
- Prisma client will work for queries

## Validation (Backend)

```typescript
import { IsString, IsOptional, IsEnum } from "class-validator";

export class CreateMyEntityDto {
  @IsString()
  name: string;

  @IsOptional()
  @IsEnum(["active", "inactive"])
  status?: "active" | "inactive";
}
```

## CORS Configuration

Already configured in `apps/backend/src/main.ts`:

```typescript
app.enableCors({
  origin: ["http://localhost:3000", "http://localhost:3001"],
  credentials: true,
});
```

## ESLint Rules

- `@typescript-eslint/no-explicit-any`: error
- TypeScript strict mode: enabled
- Must have zero linting errors

## Quick Reference

### File Locations

- **Shared Types**: `packages/shared/src/index.ts`
- **Prisma Schema**: `apps/backend/prisma/schema.prisma`
- **Backend Modules**: `apps/backend/src/[module-name]/`
- **Site Manager Components**: `apps/site-manager/src/components/`
- **Dispatcher Components**: `apps/dispatcher/src/components/`

### Ports

- Backend: 4000
- Site Manager: 3000
- Dispatcher: 3001
- PostgreSQL: 5432

### Import Paths

- Shared types: `import type { MyType } from 'shared'`
- Prisma client: `import { PrismaClient } from '@prisma/client'`

## Interview Strategy

1. **Read user story carefully** (2 min)
2. **Define types in shared package** (3 min)
3. **Create database table** (2 min)
4. **Implement backend** (15 min)
5. **Implement Site Manager** (15 min)
6. **Implement Dispatcher** (15 min)
7. **Test and verify** (8 min)

**Priority:** Working code > Perfect code. Get it working, then refine.

## Common Pitfalls to Avoid

1. ❌ Don't try Prisma migrations (permissions issue)
2. ❌ Don't forget to build shared package after type changes
3. ❌ Don't use `any` type (ESLint will fail)
4. ❌ Don't forget CORS is only for localhost:3000 and localhost:3001
5. ❌ Don't forget to import types from 'shared' package
6. ❌ Don't use relative imports for shared types

## Success Criteria Checklist

- [ ] Types defined in shared package
- [ ] Database table created
- [ ] Backend endpoints working (test with curl)
- [ ] Site Manager displays data
- [ ] Dispatcher displays data
- [ ] TypeScript compiles with no errors
- [ ] ESLint passes with zero errors
- [ ] All apps running simultaneously

This is the context for rapid feature development during a 60-minute technical interview.
